e was the one who  arranged for the deaths of danny's  parents david wenham is great as meacham  who delves deeper into insanity as the  season continues caught between iron  fist and the hand one of is likely best  known as boromir's more resilient  brother pharamir in the lord of the  rings films so it's refreshingly  unsettling to see him in a role that  pushes so hard in the other direction  it's too bad the season as a whole  wasn't as good as wenham's performance  alyssa jones played by janet mcteer  never really had much of a chance in  jessica jones's second season we learned  she survived the car crash that killed  her son and husband after which she was  nursed back to health and given powers  by the scientist carl malus by the time  melissa and jessica are reunited  alyssa's dedication to malice reaches a  manic pitch making her dangerous to  anyone near her especially after malice  dies after the much more cerebral and  emotional threat of kilgrave and jessica  jones's first season someone who could  pose more of a physical challenge to the  hero was the obvious choice and mcteer  is wonderful in the role she brings a  fierceness to alyssa that makes you  believe she's capable of anything  including hurting or even killing the  daughter she's just been reunited with  the assassin john pilgrim played by josh  stewart is singular in the ranks of  punisher villains this is for no other  reason than the fact that the guy  actually survives his clash with frank  castle with his priest's collar and the  unsettling calm with which he doles out  violence pilgrim is one of the most  chilling and disturbing villains to show  up in the punisher or any of marvel's  netflix shows we eventually learn that  as skilled as he is at killing pilgrim  is far from being a conscienceless  killer a former member of the aryan  brotherhood pilgrim eventually saw the  evil of his ways converted to  christianity and became a pastor his  bloody rampage through the second season  of the punisher is the result of the  manipulative schultz's keeping his  children hostage it's pilgrim's  dedication to his family that convinces  frank to spare his life in spite of his  crimes  trish walker is perhaps the most tragic  character in any of marvel's netflix  series when we meet her in the first  season of jessica jones she is the  titular hero's best friend and the  survivor of a horrible assault as the  series continues her desire to be more  like jessica leads her to increasingly  dangerous extremes unfortunately this  includes her taking the same addicting  medications that gave the late will  simpson his enhanced abilities surprised  to find herself with powers walker goes  down roads she can't turn back from in  the show's final season she becomes a  self-styled vigilante but her time as a  crime fighter leaves a lot to be desired  among other things she accidentally  causes one attacker to fall on her own  weapon and flees the scene rather than  helping she kills gregory salinger just  before the series finale and the final  battle of jessica jones proves to be  between jones and walker  william rollins played by paul schultz  is precisely the kind of guy frank  castle was born to kill when castle  first meets rollins in afghanistan the  cia agent seems like someone castle is  destined to lock horns with this is even  before castle learns that rollins and  schooner are using their squad to  smuggle heroin back to the united states  it's also rollins who orders the hit on  castle's life leading to deaths of his  wife and their two children so  inevitably it is rollins who meets his  own brutal end at castle's hands before  the punisher's first season is over with  his freezing glare and permanent scowl  paul schultz is utterly believable as  the corrupt operative who left his  conscience far behind long ago he's the  perfect villain for the punisher's  inaugural season and his heir of cold  arrogance clashes wonderfully with the  more likable vil