ough  skill and careful planning mary wipes  the floor with dany rand in their first  fight on a subway platform in target  iron fist  madame gao played by wai ching-ho is one  of the most dangerous people you'll meet  in marvel's netflix shows she presents  herself as a physically frail elderly  woman in order to give enemies and  allies alike a false sense of security  she prefers to work from the shadows  letting her actions speak for her and  foregoing the noise and bravado of other  bad guys while she tends to be a puppet  master more than anything else we learn  in the defenders that gal has physical  abilities that allow her to go  toe-to-toe with iron fist  not only is madame gao one of the  strongest pieces of connective tissue  throughout marvel's netflix series she's  perhaps the absolute last person you  want to mess with she may not lash out  in aggressive and bloody ways but she'll  give you that wicked smile and just wait  until the time is right  in the first half of luke cage's first  season mariah dillard wants harlem to  see her as the legitimate face of the  stove's family so she allows cornell to  lord over the criminal elements of the  neighborhood things change when he  implies the sexual abuse dillard endured  at the hands of her uncle was consensual  she kills cornell in his club and  supported by the manipulative shades  soon becomes the queen of crime in  harlem alfree woodard may have already  had a role in the mcu as a grieving  mother in 2016's captain america civil  war however her performance in luke cage  overrides any concerns a continuity  stickler might have through woodard  mariah is a tortured villain haunted by  the abuse she suffered from her criminal  family her rage and pain is bubbling at  the surface of every scene and she's  merciless enough to leave no mystery as  to how she could ever be a threat to a  man with bulletproof skin  few of marvel's netflix villains could  leave such a lasting impression as  jessica jones's 